Add an averaging-count control to Scope Grab.

The panel already exposes :ACQuire:TYPE, so AVER can be selected -- but the
number of averages is not reachable, which makes AVER mean "whatever count the
scope happened to be left on". For ILC the count is the single number that sets
the convergence floor, and it belongs in the metadata file with everything else.

The settings panel is generic, so this is one line in each of two lists.

--- a/scope_grab.py
+++ b/scope_grab.py
@@ GLOBAL_SETTINGS
     ("Acquisition", ":ACQuire:TYPE", "choice", ("NORM", "AVER", "HRES", "PEAK")),
+    ("Averages", ":ACQuire:COUNt", "num", None),
 ]

--- a/scope_grab.py
+++ b/scope_grab.py
@@ Scope.metadata
             f"acquisition type   : {s(':ACQuire:TYPE')}",
+            f"acquisition count  : {s(':ACQuire:COUNt')}",
             f"timebase s/div     : {s(':TIMebase:SCALe')}",
